id,category,question,expected_answer,expected_source,expected_section
1,breach,"How long does a PIC have to notify the NPC of a personal data breach?","Within 72 hours upon knowledge of, or reasonable belief of, a personal data breach requiring notification.",NPC-16-03,"Sec. 18"
2,breach,"Is notifying the NPC and notifying affected data subjects the same obligation?","No. They are treated as separate obligations; both must be done within the 72-hour window.",IRR-10173,"Rule IX, Sec. 38"
3,breach,"When is delay in breach notification not allowed at all?","When the breach involves at least 100 data subjects, or when disclosure of sensitive personal information will harm or adversely affect the data subject.",NPC-16-03,"Sec. 18"
4,breach,"Ilang oras ang deadline para sabihan ang mga customer na naapektuhan ng data breach?","72 oras mula sa pagkaalam o reasonable belief na nangyari ang breach.",NPC-16-03,"Sec. 18"
5,breach,"Where are personal data breach notifications submitted to the NPC?","Through the Data Breach Notification Management System (DBNMS) online platform, which is also used for Annual Security Incident Reports.",NPC-16-03,"Sec. 17"
6,breach,"What counts as 'other information' that can make a breach notifiable even if it is not sensitive personal information?","Information such as data on the financial or economic situation of the data subject, usernames and passwords and other login data, biometric data, and copies of identification documents or licenses.",NPC-16-03,"Sec. 3"
7,security,"Which NPC circular sets the minimum security requirements for personal data, and who does it cover?","NPC Circular 2023-06 on Security of Personal Data in the Government and Private Sector; it applies to both private and public sector entities.",NPC-2023-06,"Sec. 1"
8,registration,"Which circular governs registration of a data processing system and designation of a DPO?","NPC Circular 2022-04, which covers registration of personal data processing systems, notification of automated decision-making or profiling, DPO designation, and the NPC Seal of Registration.",NPC-2022-04,"Sec. 1"
9,cctv,"May CCTV kami sa office. Anong issuance ang sumasaklaw dito?","NPC Circular 2024-02, which provides the updated policy framework on the use of closed-circuit television (CCTV) systems.",NPC-2024-02,"Sec. 1"
10,certification,"What are the prerequisites for the Philippine Privacy Mark certification?","They are set out in NPC Circular 2023-05 on the Philippine Privacy Mark Certification Program.",NPC-2023-05,"Sec. 1"
11,lending,"We run a lending app. Can we access our borrowers' phone contact lists?","Processing of personal data for loan-related transactions is governed by NPC Circular 20-01 as amended by NPC Circular 2022-02, which restricts contact-list access and permits only proportional metadata subject to stated conditions.",NPC-2022-02,"Sec. 3"
12,design,"Is a confusing cookie banner that pushes users to accept a privacy issue?","Deceptive design patterns are addressed in NPC Advisory 2023-01, which sets guidelines on them.",NPC-ADV-2023-01,"Sec. 1"
13,governance,"Who administers and implements the Data Privacy Act?","The National Privacy Commission, an independent body created under RA 10173, attached to the DICT.",RA-10173,"Sec. 7"
14,scope,"Does the Data Privacy Act apply to personal data of foreign nationals processed in the Philippines?","Yes. The Act covers personal information of persons whose data is being processed in the Philippines, including data from foreign jurisdictions processed here.",RA-10173,"Sec. 4"
15,refusal-control,"How much is the maximum GDPR fine for a company in Germany?","REFUSE — outside the corpus. The assistant should say it does not have this and point to the NPC or counsel.",NONE,NONE
16,refusal-control,"Sino ang mananalo sa eleksyon sa 2028?","REFUSE — outside the corpus and not a compliance question.",NONE,NONE
